+# Raumata dual-protocol stack
+
+This tree can run Meshtastic and MeshCore at the same time on the Heltec V3's
+single SX1262.  The goal is to let one radio participate in a Meshtastic mesh
+and a MeshCore mesh without a hardware modification.
+
+## Shared PHY
+
+A LoRa receiver has one demodulator configuration at a time.  Meshtastic's
+default ANZ LongFast profile (BW250/SF11/CR5, sync word `0x2B`) and MeshCore's
+Australia preset (916.575 MHz, BW62.5/SF7) cannot be received simultaneously.
+
+Raumata therefore puts both stacks on the **same PHY**: the frequency,
+bandwidth, spreading factor, coding rate, sync word, preamble length, and CRC
+settings configured for Meshtastic.  MeshCore's radio parameters are mirrored
+from Meshtastic and `CMD_SET_RADIO_PARAMS` is rejected by the companion
+interface.
+
+This means the MeshCore side is a *shared-PHY sub-mesh*: MeshCore peers must be
+configured to the same PHY.  It does not talk to standard MeshCore nodes using
+the public 916.575 MHz/SF7 preset unless those nodes are reconfigured too.
+
+## Frame demultiplexing
+
+MeshCore frames are prepended with the four-byte transport tag `RAUM` before
+they reach the radio.  Received frames beginning with the tag are stripped and
+handed to MeshCore; everything else is passed to Meshtastic unchanged.  The tag
+is transport-level only, so MeshCore's packet format and cryptography are
+unmodified.
+
+## Radio ownership
+
+`RadioLibInterface` gains a raw-frame sink and a raw transmit path:
+
+- RX: the sink runs after `readData()` and before Meshtastic header parsing.
+  MeshCore frames are queued for `MeshCoreRadio::recvRaw()`.
+- TX: MeshCore and Meshtastic serialize access with a mutex and an owner flag.
+  If Meshtastic is transmitting, MeshCore keeps its frame pending and retries
+  from `MeshCoreRadio::loop()`.  Meshtastic's TX queue waits while MeshCore owns
+  the radio.
+
+Both stacks share one antenna and one airtime budget, so collisions and
+occasional dropped frames are expected under heavy load.
+
+## MeshCore node
+
+`src/raumata/MeshCoreNode.*` is a `BaseChatMesh` subclass with:
+
+- an ed25519 identity persisted in NVS (`raumata/mc_id`);
+- up to eight channels persisted in NVS (`raumata/mc_ch`), defaulting to the
+  MeshCore public channel;
+- adverts on boot and every 15 minutes;
+- direct and group text messages;
+- a queue of received messages for the companion protocol.
+
+Contacts learned from adverts are kept in RAM and are not persisted yet.
+
+## Companion interface
+
+A USB-serial mux parses both Meshtastic (`0x94 0xC3`) and MeshCore (`<`) frame
+framing.  MeshCore companion apps can use the USB port; Meshtastic's PhoneAPI
+continues to work on the same port.  While MeshCore companion mode is active,
+Meshtastic debug text and FromRadio writes are suppressed so the app sees a
+clean frame stream.
+
+The companion implementation covers app start, device query, time sync,
+contacts, channels, sending/receiving text, self-adverts, and battery/storage.
+Unsupported or radio-changing commands return `ERR_CODE_UNSUPPORTED_CMD`.
+MeshCore BLE companion is not implemented in this series.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+pio run -e heltec-v3-dual
+```
+
+The environment vendors MeshCore's core under `lib/meshcore` and adds the
+`rweather/Crypto` and `densaugeo/base64` libraries for MeshCore's AES/SHA-256
+and channel-key handling.  Only the Heltec V3 profile is verified.
